# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# BildyApp API — curl examples (http://localhost:3000)
# Paste tokens / ids where noted. Run API: npm run dev
#
# VS Code REST Client: see requests/user.http, client.http, project.http,
# deliverynote.http (variables {{baseUrl}}, {{token}}, …).
#
# OpenAPI Try it out: http://localhost:3000/api-docs (not rate-limited)
# Tests: npm test (in-memory MongoDB; see README.md)
#
# Auth chain for /api/client|project|deliverynote: Bearer JWT + verified email + company.
# Public: POST /api/user/register, /login, /refresh (no Bearer).
#
# Socket.IO (same port): auth: { token: "<accessToken>" } or Authorization Bearer.
# Events: client:new, project:new, deliverynote:new, deliverynote:signed
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Quick smoke — register (copy full blocks from requests/*.http for each route)
curl -sS -X POST "http://localhost:3000/api/user/register" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"admin@test.com","password":"password123"}'

# Full curl catalog previously in this file now lives alongside REST files; see:
#   requests/user.http
#   requests/client.http
#   requests/project.http
#   requests/deliverynote.http
